  "worked_solution": "Let the function $f(x,y)$ be defined as\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\frac{x(xy-1)}{y}.\n$$\n\nThe function $f(x,y)$ is continuous except when the denominator is zero. However, the point $(2,1)$ does not cause the denominator to vanish, so we can calculate the limit by substituting $(2,1)$ into the function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (2,1)}\\frac{x(xy-1)}{y} & =\\frac{2(2\\cdot 1-1)}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(1)}{1} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
